I am slightly higher than the crowd on 1 major hurricane. As of the [latest NHC outlook](https://prod-east-nhc.woc.noaa.gov/text/refresh/MIATWOAT%2Bshtml/050508_MIATWOAT.shtml), a surface trough has developed along Mexico in the southwestern Gulf. NHC says a tropical depression could form during the second half of this week and has raised genesis probabilities to:&#x20;

* 10% within 48 hours
* 50% within 7 days

But the crucial phrase is that environmental conditions are expected to be only “marginally conducive.”&#x20;

There is some ensemble support too. [Ryan Maue](https://weather.substack.com/p/october-4-2026-sunday-tropical-update) notes that many ECMWF ensemble members produce a tropical storm or hurricane in the Gulf, although the deterministic ECMWF was considerably less aggressive.&#x20;
